1
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:07,180
Using language Reading, acting and speaking

2
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:12,320
The million pound bank note Act 1,

3
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:14,640
scene 4

4
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:19,480
Outside a restaurant, Henry looks at the envelope without opening it

5
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,800
and decides to go in.

6
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:24,140
He sits down at a table next to the front window.

7
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:30,000
That one's reserved. This way, please.

8
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:32,720
Take this gentleman's order, Horace.

9
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:40,860
I'd like some ham and eggs and a nice big steak. Make it extra thick.

10
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,460
I'd also like a cup of coffee and a pineapple dessert.

11
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:49,040
Right, sir. I'm afraid it'll cost a large amount of money.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,920
I understand. And I'll have a large glass of beer.

13
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,080
Okay.

14
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:58,540
My goodness, why, look at him. He's like a wolf.

15
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,100
We'll see if he's clever as a wolf,

16
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:01,560
eh?

17
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,760
Waiter, same thing again, please. Oh,

18
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:06,680
and another beer.

19
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:08,720
Again? Everything?

20
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,340
Yes, that's right. Anything wrong?

21
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:17,980
No, not at all. He's asked for more of the same.

22
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:22,540
Well, it is well known that Americans like to eat a lot.

23
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:28,160
Well, we'll have to take a chance. Go ahead and let him have it.

24
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:31,480
All right. That's two orders of ham and eggs,

25
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,040
two extra thick steaks,

26
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:37,100
two large glasses of beer, two cups of coffee and two desserts.

27
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,860
Would you mind waiting just a few minutes?

28
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:41,640
What's there to wait for?

29
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,580
All right, Horace. I'll take care of this.

30
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:47,540
That was a wonderful meal.

31
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:51,200
It's amazing how much pleasure you get out of the simple things in life,

32
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,200
especially if you can't have them for a while.

33
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:58,020
Yes, very interesting. Now, perhaps,

34
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,980
sir, if you pay your bill, I can help the other customers.

35
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:05,180
Well, I see it's two o'clock.

36
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:13,240
I'm very sorry, but I don't have anything smaller.

37
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:17,400
Well, just one moment.

38
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:22,540
Maggie, look. Do you think it's genuine?

39
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:26,600
Oh, dear. I don't know. I simply don't know.

40
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:31,840
Well, I did hear that the Bank of England had issued two notes in this amount.

41
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:35,080
Anyway, I don't think it can be a fake.

42
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:39,460
People would pay too much attention to a banknote of this amount.

43
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,800
No thief would want that to happen.

44
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,320
But he's in rags.

45
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:47,560
Perhaps he's a very strange rich man.

46
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,940
Um, why, yes, that must be it.

47
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:55,680
And you put him in the back of the restaurant. Go and see him at once.

48
00:02:56,560 --> 00:03:02,080
I'm so sorry, sir, so sorry, but I cannot change this banknote.

49
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,660
But it's all I have on me.

50
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:08,320
Oh, please, don't worry, sir. It doesn't matter at all.

51
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,480
We're so very glad that you even entered our little eating place.

52
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:16,120
Indeed, sir, I hope you'll come here whenever you like.

53
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:19,660
Well, that's very kind of you.

54
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,440
Kind, sir? No, it's kind of you.

55
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:26,340
You must come whenever you want and have whatever you like.

56
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,520
Just having you sit here is a great honor.

57
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:33,220
As for the bill, sir, please forget it.

58
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:37,200
Forget it? Well, thank you very much.

59
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,100
That's very nice of you.

60
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,540
Oh, it's for us to thank you, sir,

61
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:44,360
and I do, sir, from the bottom of my heart.
